  "inversion_definition_review": {
    "probe_definition": "adjacent cached free blocks a, b (a evicted first) with end_a < end_b, or end_a == end_b with a SWA and b MLA, over the whole free queue",
    "pr_stated_purpose": [
      "test docstring: 'Cached blocks (block_hash is not None) sit in monotonically decreasing order of token offset (end_token) from the LRU head of free_block_queue to the MRU tail'; 'Consequently, partial eviction from the BlockPool always evicts the newest tail blocks first and preserves the root prefix blocks.'",
      "test code comment: 'monotonically NON-INCREASING from head (evict first) to tail (evict last) across all cached blocks'",
      "README: 'root checkpoints (512, 8,192) sit at the MRU tail (evicted last)'",
      "test comment on turn 2: 'early SWA checkpoints at 8192 etc. are skipped by SlidingWindowManager.add_local_computed_blocks!' (the target is blocks outside the finished request's run)"
    ],
